  "notes": "Used for both physical fastening and abstract concepts like fixed rates or assigned positions. The noun form {固定|こてい} is very common as a modifier.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {固定|こてい}{費|ひ}: fixed cost\n- {固定|こてい}{金利|きんり}: fixed interest rate\n- {固定|こてい}{電話|でんわ}: landline phone\n- {固定|こてい}{席|せき}: assigned seat\n- {固定|こてい}{概念|がいねん}: fixed idea, preconception\n- {固定|こてい}{資産|しさん}: fixed assets\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {留|と}める: to fasten, to pin — everyday word for attaching with clips, pins, etc.\n- {固定|こてい}する: to fix in place — more formal, implies making something permanently or securely immovable\n- {据|す}え{付|つ}ける: to install, to set in place — used for installing equipment or fixtures",
